  "response_text": "Once the function fell out of its last instruction and executed\u00a0BX LR, the core would load whatever value we pre-stuffed into the thread\u2019s link register. In our setup that LR is just a sentinel (e.g.,\u00a00xFFFFFFFD\u00a0or\u00a00xDEADDEAD), not a real code address, so the CPU would branch to an unmapped or mis-aligned location, immediately triggering a fault that escalates into a HardFault. Because the scheduler assumes threads never \u201creturn\u201d the normal C way, letting one do so leaves the processor with nowhere valid to go and crashes the program.\\n",
